{"cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "ccr-6c7564b1-fmlt1w", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "The task rate card can change. Use the current rate card shown in\nthe platform when estimating task costs rather than embedding model prices in\nclient code.\n\n## Frameboy sessions\n\nA Frameboy session in Atlas Studio runs for up to a minute and costs 500\ncredits ($0.50), charged once, after it ends. It draws on the same credits as\nother Studio work. A session is free if it plays for less than 5 seconds, or if\nit ends because its server stopped responding.\n\nAn account without enough credits cannot start a session: the request returns\n`402 Payment Required` with `code` set to `CREDITS_UNAVAILABLE`, and no session\n== atlas-generate 278 lines\nGenerate posed views from image, depth, and camera context.\n`atlasGenerate` generates posed RGB views at target cameras from one or more\nposed RGBD context frames. Use it to see the same scene from new camera\n[atlasChisel](/depth-guided-generation#restyle-a-scene).\n## Prepare RGBD context\nEvery `contextFrames` entry requires an `imageAsset`, `depth`, and `camera`.\nresponse. All context cameras must declare the same width and height; that\nresolution may differ from the target cameras' resolution.\nframing against its depth and camera before supplying it as context. Omitting\nKeep each context image and its maps on the grid described by its camera.\nTarget cameras specify the generated output size. The aspect-ratio requirement\nAll target cameras must share one size: 1280 × 720, 960 × 720, 528 × 704, or\n![The four supported Atlas Generate target sizes drawn at the same scale: 1280 by 720, 960 by 720, 528 by 704, and 720 by 1280.](/media/atlas-diagrams/atlas-target-resolutions.svg \"All targets in one request use the same size. Context views may use a different resolution.\")\nContext depth is required even when `returnDepth` is `false`.\n== atlas-walkthrough 1094 lines\nPrepare context frames, choose target cameras, and build a request for new views.\nAtlas generates views from posed RGBD context frames. Each context frame brings together an image, its depth map, and the camera that captured it.\nKeep image, depth, and camera coordinates aligned. Supply at least one context frame and one target camera. Asset references in the example are placeholders; replace them with assets in your project before using the request.\nGenerates posed views from RGBD context at explicit target cameras, with optional reconstructed output depth.\n  \"contextFrames\": [\n        \"assetId\": \"asset_context_image\"\n          \"assetId\": \"asset_context_depth\"\n  \"prompt\": \"A quiet sunlit room\",\n    \"promptUsed\": \"A cinematic world with clear depth, coherent geometry, and no people\",\n        \"description\": \"Generates posed views from RGBD context at explicit target cameras, with optional reconstructed output depth.\",\n              \"description\": \"Block for the operation to finish before returning, up to the server wait cap. Returns the Operation either way — done with a response if it finished in time, otherwise still running.\",\n            \"description\": \"Block for the operation to finish before returning, up to the server wait cap. Returns the Operation either way — done with a response if it finished in time, otherwise still running.\"\n          \"contextFrames\": {\n            \"title\": \"Contextframes\",\n== depth-guided-generation 384 lines\nGenerate posed RGB views at target cameras from posed depth and a prompt.\n`atlasChisel` generates posed RGB views at a set of target cameras from\noptional posed depth at those cameras, a required text prompt, and optional\n  from a blockout or an existing scene and a prompt describing the desired\n  appearance. For a new look, follow [Restyle a scene](#restyle-a-scene).\n  To generate from a prompt alone, send camera-only `targetFrames` and omit\n  `contextFrames`.\n- 