iption": "Bundle-adjust the estimated cameras against dense matches before answering. The backbone's poses are good to about half a degree, which is enough to reconstruct from and not enough to refine against: the residual shows up as blur wherever two views disagree. The solve anchors on the depth this task has just produced, so it costs a matcher pass and a solve rather than another reconstruction, and it needs two or more frames. A solve that moves the cameras further than the guards allow is thrown away and the unrefined reconstruction is returned, which is a success rather than an error.", "title": "Refineposes", "type": "boolean"}, "targetResolution": {"anyOf": [{"maxItems": 2, "minItems": 2, "prefixItems": [{"type": "integer"}, {"type": "integer"}], "type": "array"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Return the depth, confidence and camera intrinsics on this (width, height) pixel grid: one of 1280 by 720, 720 by 1280, 960 by 720 or 528 by 704, the grids the depth model serves. The reconstruction is scaled to cover the requested size and center-cropped to it, so the result is exactly the size asked for and never stretched, and the intrinsics are updated with it -- unprojecting the returned depth with the returned camera gives the same geometry either way. A requested aspect that differs from the frames' costs field of view, since the crop is what makes the size exact, and centroidWorld then describes the cropped view. Omit it (or pass null) and a multi-view capture with camera translation comes back on whichever of those four grids is closest in aspect to the frames: smaller frames are scaled up onto it, and other aspects (square or 3:2, for example) are center-cropped onto the closest one, with squares going to 960 by 720. A single image or a capture without camera translation comes back on the reconstruction backend's native grid. Set it when a later step needs a particular grid: atlasGenerate, for example, needs context frames with the same aspect as its target cameras.", "title": "Targetresolution"}, "webhookUrl": {"anyOf": [{"maxLength": 2048, "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Where Atlas POSTs one signed task.succeeded or task.failed event when this operation finishes; retried for 24 hours. Verify the signature with the public keys at /.well-known/webhooks/jwks.json. Cannot be combined with ?wait=true. https on port 443 only, no IP literals. Developer API only.", "title": "Webhookurl"}}, "required": ["frames"], "title": "Images2PosedRGBDRequest", "type": "object"}}, "required": ["project_id", "request", "idempotency_key"], "title": "runArguments", "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__World_Labs_Atlas__images2PosedRGBD"}], "type": "deferred_tools_record"}, "cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "ccr-6c7564b1-fmlt1w", "isSidechain": false, "parentUuid": "08cd8f7e-d43a-4bb6-8187-4c1d6057d3fe", "sessionId": "8ca76314-247f-58db-ab0f-3465514af18e", "timestamp": "2026-11-18T16:53:39.465Z", "type": "attachment", "userType": "external", "uuid": "4c0cca1f-b45a-4a63-97eb-453c1b36015f", "version": "2.1.327"}
